## Quick start

```bash
bash scripts/setup.sh
```

`setup.sh` will: check the tools above, install the Python dependencies{{ " and, if it exists, the frontend" if project_layout == 'product' }}, install the pre-commit hook{{ ", initialise DVC" if use_ml }}, and create `.env` from `.env.example`. It never installs anything system-wide.

Dependencies are not written by hand: they were resolved to their latest versions when the project was generated, pinned exactly in `{{ py_root }}pyproject.toml` and locked in `{{ py_root }}uv.lock`{{ " (and `frontend/package.json` and `package-lock.json`)" if project_layout == 'product' }}. Add more with `uv add <pkg>` (or `uv add --dev <pkg>`){{ " from `backend/`, and `npm install <pkg>` from `frontend/`" if project_layout == 'product' }}; both pin the exact version.

