## Docs

This project keeps several kinds of documentation, each with its own purpose, scope, and lifecycle -- don't mix them up.

| Location | What it holds | Scope | Written by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `CONTEXT.md` | Project glossary -- resolved terminology only, no implementation details. | Project-wide (or one per bounded context, via `CONTEXT-MAP.md`); reused across every spec. | `domain-modeling` / `grill-with-docs` |
| `docs/ADRs/` | Architecture decision records -- hard-to-reverse, non-obvious decisions with a real trade-off behind them. | Project-wide, same lifecycle as `CONTEXT.md`. | `domain-modeling` |
| `docs/specs/<type>-<yyyy_mm>-<name>/` | One folder per spec (`<type>` is `feat`, `fix`, or `refactor`): `SPEC.md` (problem, solution, decisions), `PLAN.md` (a seam-organized task breakdown), and `REPORT.md` (what `implement` did, updated in place). All three sit directly in the folder. | Per spec -- that piece of work's own task list and outcome, not shared with any other spec. | `/spec`, `implement` |
| `docs/debug/` | One report per bug investigation, `<yyyy_mm>-<slug>.md`: the hypotheses tested, the diagnosis and the fix. Separate from specs because one investigation can touch several of them. | Per bug. | `debugger` |
| `docs/clarifications/` | Personal scratch notes for understanding a new topic while working on a task. Gitignored: never committed, and not read by the skills unless you point at a file. | Just you. | You |
| `docs/build/` | Generated API docs (gitignored). | Rebuilt on demand. | `pdoc`, via `make docs` |

See [.claude/skills/spec/SKILL.md](.claude/skills/spec/SKILL.md) for the full spec-to-implementation workflow, and [.claude/skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md](.claude/skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md) for how `CONTEXT.md` and ADRs get built and maintained.

