## Logging

Logging is configured in code, in `utils/logger.py`: console plus a rotating file, set up on the first call to `get_logger`. Set `LOG_LEVEL` (for example `DEBUG`) in the environment to change the level; the default is `INFO`.

```python
from {{ package_name }}.utils.logger import get_logger

logger = get_logger(__name__)
logger.info("Starting process")
```

Logs are written to `logs/` at the repo root (gitignored), whichever directory the process starts in. The file handler rotates at 10 MB, keeping 5 backups.

