## CI/CD

| Workflow | Trigger | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `ci.yml` | push / PR to `main` | Python: `make lint-py`, `make format-check`, `make typecheck`, `make test-py`.{{ ' Frontend: lint, test and build.' if project_layout == 'product' }} Cancels superseded runs |
| `markdown.yml` | push / PR touching `.md` files | markdownlint and relative-link check |

CI calls the same `make` targets you run locally, so a green `make lint test` means a green pipeline.

`.github/dependabot.yaml` is gitignored by default. To get monthly dependency update PRs, remove its line from `.gitignore` and commit the file. Updates are grouped (dev tooling and runtime, minor and patch batched, one PR per major), and the Ruff version in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` has to be bumped by hand to match `pyproject.toml`.

